------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Calling SevenZFile.read() on empty SevenZArchiveEntry throws IllegalStateException\nType: Bug | Priority: Minor | Status: Resolved | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nI'm pretty sure COMPRESS-340 breaks reading empty archive entries. When calling getNextEntry() and that entry has no content, the code jumps into the first block at line 830 (SevenZFile.class), clearing the deferredBlockStreams. When calling entry.read(...) afterwards an IllegalStateException (\"No current 7z entry (call getNextEntry() first).\") is thrown. IMHO, there should be another check for entry.getSize() == 0.\n\nThis worked correctly up until 1.10.\n\nComments:\n\n[Stefan Bodewig]: Thank you for creating a new issue for this.\n\nI had seen your comments in COMPRESS-340 but wanted to create a testcase before opening a new issue - unfortunately I still need to find a time slot to do this.\n\n[Stefan Bodewig]: You are correct, I see what you describe. At least for my simplistic archive the situation is fixed with git comit d050157 - it would be good if you could confirm this with your own archives.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.sevenz.SevenZFile (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.sevenz.SevenZFile (fixed)\n@@ -899,6 +899,9 @@\n     }\n     \n     private InputStream getCurrentStream() throws IOException {\n+        if (archive.files[currentEntryIndex].getSize() == 0) {\n+            return new ByteArrayInputStream(new byte[0]);\n+        }\n         if (deferredBlockStreams.isEmpty()) {\n             throw new IllegalStateException(\"No current 7z entry (call getNextEntry() first).\");\n         }"
